Is a Warning Sign for the US: Historians\",\"description\":\"Jan 1, 2023 · He was followed by Yuri Andropov, who died in 1984 at 69. Andropov's successor, Konstantin Chernenko, died in 1985 at 73. Fast-forward to 2022.\",\"url\":\"https://www.businessinsider.com/soviet-gerontocracy-collapse-cautionary-tale-united-states-2022-9\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"85\",\"title\":\"Russia - Perestroika, Glasnost, Reforms - Britannica\",\"description\":\"When Gorbachev became head of the Communist Party in 1985, he launched perestroika (“restructuring”). His team was more heavily Russian than that of his ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/place/Russia/The-Gorbachev-era-perestroika-and-glasnost\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"86\",\"title\":\"Perestroika: Glasnost, Definition \u0026 Soviet Union - History.com\",\"description\":\"Apr 14, 2010 · While Gorbachev had instituted these reforms to jumpstart the sluggish Soviet economy, many of them had the opposite effect. The agricultural ...Early Attempts at Reform · Economic Reforms Backfire · Political Reforms Under...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/articles/perestroika-and-glasnost\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"87\",\"title\":\"The Dissolution of the Soviet Union: Then and Now - Atlantic Council\",\"description\":\"Nov 21, 2016 · They were written and signed on December 8, 1991, in Belarus's Belovezhskaya Pushcha. Shushkevich told the story of how the accords came to be.\",\"url\":\"https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/the-dissolution-of-the-soviet-union-then-and-now/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"88\",\"title\":\"The Collapse of the Soviet Union - Office of the Historian\",\"description\":\"The unsuccessful August 1991 coup against Gorbachev sealed the fate of the Soviet Union. Planned by hard-line Communists, the coup diminished Gorbachev's power ...\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/milestones/1989-1992/collapse-soviet-union\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"89\",\"title\":\"[PD