n-ukraine-from-2014-to-24-february-2022/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"142\",\"title\":\"Crimea referendum: Voters 'back Russia union' - BBC News\",\"description\":\"Mar 16, 2014 · Election officials say 95.5% of Crimean voters back joining Russia in a disputed referendum, with half the ballots counted.\",\"url\":\"https://www.bbc.com/news/world-europe-26606097\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"143\",\"title\":\"Ukraine crisis: Protesters declare Donetsk 'republic' - BBC News\",\"description\":\"Apr 7, 2014 · Pro-Russian protesters who seized the regional government building in the Ukrainian city of Donetsk are reported to have declared a people's republic.\",\"url\":\"https://www.bbc.com/news/world-europe-26919928\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"144\",\"title\":\"Ukraine separatists declare independence | News - Al Jazeera\",\"description\":\"May 12, 2014 · Leaders of eastern Donetsk and Luhansk regions declare independence after claiming victory in Sunday's self-rule vote.\",\"url\":\"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2014/5/12/ukraine-separatists-declare-independence\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"145\",\"title\":\"Conflict in Ukraine's Donbas: A Visual Explainer\",\"description\":\"The visual explainer below focuses not on the full-scale escalation that began on 24 February, but on fighting in the Donbas region of eastern Ukraine that ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.crisisgroup.org/visual-explainers/conflict-ukraines-donbas-visual-explainer\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"146\",\"title\":\"What are the Minsk agreements on the Ukraine conflict? | Reuters\",\"description\":\"Feb 21, 2022 · Its provisions included prisoner exchanges, deliveries of humanitarian aid and the withdrawal of heavy weapons, five months into a conflict that ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/what-are-minsk-agreements-ukraine-conflict-2022-02-21/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"147\",\"title\":\"Ukraine, Russia, and the Minsk agreements: A post-mortem | ECFR\",\"description\":\"Feb 19, 2024 · The Minsk agreements were signed by Ukraine, Russia, and the OSCE special representative in September 2014 and February 2015.\",\"url\":\"https://ecfr.eu/article/ukraine-russia-and-the-minsk-agreements-a-post-mortem/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"148\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Conflict-related civilian casualties in Ukraine1\",\"description\":\"Jan 27, 2022 · In total, from 14 April 2014 to 31 December 2021, OHCHR recorded 1,242 civilian casualties caused by mine-related incidents, ERW handling and ...\",\"url\":\"https://ukraine.un.org/sites/default/files/2022-02/Conflict-related%2520civilian%2520casualties%2520as%2520of%252031%2520December%25202021%2520%2528rev%252027%2520January%25202022%2529%2520corr%2520EN_0.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"149\",\"title\":\"Russia recognises the independence of the Donbas\",\"description\":\"Feb 22, 2022 · On 21 February, Russian President Vladimir Putin delivered an address in which he announced the recognition of the independence of two separatist para-states.\",\"url\":\"https://www.osw.waw.pl/en/publikacje/analyses/2022-02-22/russia-recognises-independence-donbas\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"150\",\"title\":\"'No other option': Excerpts of Putin's speech declaring war - Al Jazeera\",\"description\":\"Feb 24, 2022 · In the early hours of Thursday, February 24, 2022, Russian President Vladimir Putin addressed his nation, announcing a “special military ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/2/24/putins-speech-declaring-war-on-ukraine-translated-excerpts\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"151\",\"title\":\"NATO Expansion: What Gorbachev Heard - National Security Archive\",\"description\":\"Dec 12, 2017 · Declassified documents show security assurances against NATO expansion to Soviet leaders from Baker, Bush, Genscher, Kohl, Gates, Mitterrand, Thatcher, Hurd, ...\",\"url\":\"https://nsarchive.gwu.edu/briefing-book/russia-programs/2017-12-12/nato-expansion-what-gorbachev-heard-western-leaders-early\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"152\",\"title\":\"Russia-Ukraine War | Map, Casualties, Timeline, Death ... - Britannica\",\"description\":\"On February 24, 2022, Russia launched a full-scale invasion of Ukraine. Although Russian forces made significant gains in the first days of combat, Ukrainian ...The Ukrainian counterattack · Crimea · The price of Putin’s war\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/event/2022-Russian-invasion-of-Ukraine\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"153\",\"title\":\"De-bunking Russian disinformation on NATO\",\"description\":\"Oct 24, 2024 · NATO promised Russia it would not enlarge after the Cold War​​ No treaty signed by NATO Allies and Russia ever included provisions that NATO ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nato.int/cps/en/natohq/115204.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"154\",\"title\":\"Russia in Facts and Numbers\",\"description\":\"At 17,075,400 square kilometres (6,592,800 sq mi), Russia is by far the largest country in the world, covering more than a ninth of the Earth's land area.\",\"url\":\"https://canada.mid.ru/en/o_rossii/russia_in_facts_and_numbers/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"155\",\"title\":\"LAND AND GEOGRAPHY OF RUSSIA | Facts and Details\",\"description\":\"Russia is the world's largest country, spanning Europe and Asia, with flat or rolling terrain, forests, steppes, and many lakes and swamps. It has a broad  ...\",\"url\":\"https://factsanddetails.com/russia/Nature_Science_Animals/sub9_8a/entry-5052.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"156\",\"title\":\"Russia – World Regional Geography - Pressbooks.pub\",\"description\":\"The western half of Russia is generally more mountainous than the eastern half, which is mostly low-elevation plains.Missing:  highest | Show results with:highest\",\"url\":\"https://pressbooks.pub/worldgeo/chapter/russia/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"157\",\"title\":\"Russia Map - GIS Geography\",\"description\":\"The Ural Mountains split Russia into western and eastern regions. In the west, the terrain is mostly broad plain with low hills. Then to the east, it's the West ...Missing:  highest | Show results with:highest\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://gisgeography.com/russia-map/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"158\",\"title\":\"Russia Maps \u0026 Facts - World Atlas\",\"description\":\"Feb 24, 2021 · Making up the natural border between European Russia and Asia, the Ural Mountains extend from the Arctic Ocean to Kazakhstan's northern border.\",\"url\":\"https://www.worldatlas.com/maps/russia\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"159\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Physical Geography of Russia\",\"description\":\"The Caucasus Mountains reach their highest elevation at Mount Elbrus, an extinct volcano that reaches 18,510 feet. (5,642 m), Russia's highest point.\",\"url\":\"https://www.anderson.k12.ky.us/Downloads/chap14.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"160\",\"title\":\"Russian Geography - Regions of Russia\",\"description\":\"The climate is mostly continental, with average January temperatures ranging from 0 to minus five degrees Centigrade in Western European Russia to minus 40-50 ...\u003c|control11|\u003e\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://singapore.mid.ru/en/russia_and_singapore/about_russia/russian_geography_regions_of_russia/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"161\",\"title\":\"Russian FederationRUS - Country Overview\",\"description\":\"Köppen-Geiger Climate Classification Types. Tropical Climates. Af – Tropical rainforest climate; Am – Tropical monsoon climate; As/Aw – Tropical savanna climate.\",\"url\":\"https://climateknowledgeportal.worldbank.org/country/russian-federation\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"162\",\"title\":\"Lowest temperature - inhabited | Guinness World Records\",\"description\":\"The lowest temperature in the northern hemisphere is -67.7°C (-90°F), recorded in Oymyakon (63°28'N, 142°23'E; 2018 est. pop. 500) in the Sakha (Yakutia) ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/lowest-temperature-inhabited\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"163\",\"title\":\"On Today's Date: Antarctica, Siberia's Records | Weather.com\",\"description\":\"Feb 6, 2025 · O​n Feb. 6, 1933, 92 years ago, Oymyakon, Russia, plunged to minus 89.9 degrees. That still stands as the world's coldest temperature recorded ...\",\"url\":\"https://weather.com/news/weather/news/2025-02-05-on-todays-date-antarctica-record-high-2020-oymyakon-record-low-1933\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"164\",\"title\":\"Temperature Difference Across Russia Reaches 85.6 C, Almost ...\",\"description\":\"Dec 10, 2021 · Temperature contrasts in Russia reached 85.6 degrees Celsius on Wednesday, the biggest difference in a single country since 1954.Missing:  highs | Show results with:highs\",\"url\":\"https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2021/12/10/temperature-difference-across-russia-reaches-856-c-almost-breaking-world-record-a75784\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"165\",\"title\":\"Russia | National Geographic Kids\",\"description\":\"Russia has about 100,000 rivers, including some of the longest and most powerful in the world. It also has many lakes, including Europe's two largest: Ladoga ...Missing:  total | Show results with:total\",\"url\":\"https://kids.nationalgeographic.com/geography/countries/article/russia\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"166\",\"title\":\"Country with the Highest Number of Rivers\",\"description\":\"Oct 10, 2025 · Learn why Russia, with over 100,000 rivers including the Volga, Lena, Ob, Yenisei, and Amur, holds the record for the largest river network ...Missing:  length | Show results with:length\",\"url\":\"https://www.jagranjosh.com/general-knowledge/country-with-the-highest-number-of-rivers-1820003244-1\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"167\",\"title\":\"The Longest Rivers in Russia including Photos and Location\",\"description\":\"Jan 31, 2023 · While the Yenisei “proper” is usually cited as 2,167 miles long, its full river system, beginning in Mongolia, runs for 3,442 miles, draining an ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.discoveryuk.com/travel-and-exploration/the-longest-rivers-in-russia/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"168\",\"title\":\"GREAT RIVERS OF RUSSIA - Facts and Details\",\"description\":\"The Volga is the longest river in Europe. All of these rivers have complex systems of tributaries that collectively drain much of Russia's territory.WATER AND DRAINAGE IN... · Principal Rivers of Russia · Volga River · Ob River\",\"url\":\"https://factsanddetails.com/russia/Nature_Science_Animals/sub9_8a/entry-5053.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"169\",\"title\":\"Russia - Drainage - GlobalSecurity.org\",\"description\":\"Mar 31, 2017 · Forty of Russia's rivers longer than 1,000 kilometers are east of the Urals, including the three major rivers that drain Siberia as they flow ...Missing:  lengths | Show results with:lengths\",\"url\":\"https://www.globalsecurity.org/military/world/russia/geography-drainage.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"170\",\"title\":\"Lake Baikal | Location, Depth, Map, \u0026 Facts | Britannica\",\"description\":\"It is also the world's largest freshwater lake by volume, containing about one-fifth of the fresh water on Earth's surface, some 5,500 cubic miles (23,000 cubic ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/place/Lake-Baikal\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"171\",\"title\":\"Lake Baikal - Simple English Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Average depth, 744.4 m (2,442 ft). Max. depth, 1,642 m (5,387 ft). Water volume, 23,615.39 km3 (5,700 cu mi). Residence time, 330 years. Shore ...Missing:  facts | Show results with:facts\",\"url\":\"https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Baikal\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"172\",\"title\":\"Lake Baikal Facts\",\"description\":\"Lake Baikal is the deepest lake in the world with a maximum depth of 1,632m; It is also the world's largest volume of fresh water 23,000 cubic km. This means ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.lakebaikal.org/lake-baikal-facts/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"173\",\"title\":\"Russia Natural Gas Reserves, Production and Consumption Statistics\",\"description\":\"Russia holds 1,688 trillion cubic feet (Tcf) of proven gas reserves as of 2017, ranking #2 in the world and accounting for about 24.39% of the world's total gas ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.worldometers.info/gas/russia-natural-gas/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"174\",\"title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/science/natural-gas/Location-of-major-gas-fields\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"175\",\"title\":\"Russia Oil Reserves, Production and Consumption Statistics\",\"description\":\"Russia produces 11,262,746 barrels per day of oil (as of 2016) ranking #3 in the world. Russia produces every year an amount equivalent to 5.14% ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.worldometers.info/oil/russia-oil/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"176\",\"title\":\"Russia Crude Oil Production - Trading Economics\",\"description\":\"Crude Oil Production in Russia decreased to 9783 BBL/D/1K in June from 9818 BBL/D/1K in May of 2025. Crude Oil Production in Russia averaged 8651.65 BBL/D/1K ...\",\"url\":\"https://tradingeconomics.com/russia/crude-oil-production\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"177\",\"title\":\"Russia: Mining, Minerals and Fuel Resources - AZoMining\",\"description\":\"Jul 24, 2025 · Industrial Minerals: Russia is the leading global diamond producer, contributing about 20 percent of worldwide yields with annual outputs ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.azomining.com/Article.aspx?ArticleID=44\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"178\",\"title\":\"Russia - Forest Area (% Of Land Area) - Trading Economics\",\"description\":\"Forest area (% of land area) in Russia was reported at 49.78 % in 2023, according to the World Bank collection of development indicators, compiled from ...Missing:  cover | Show results with:cover\",\"url\":\"https://tradingeconomics.com/russia/forest-area-percent-of-land-area-wb-data.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"179\",\"title\":\"Mapping the world's forests: How green is our globe?\",\"description\":\"Jan 27, 2023 · A table listing the top 10 countries for forest cover. Russia is ranked at number 1 with 815 million hectares of forest cover. Image: Visual ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.weforum.org/stories/2023/01/mapping-worlds-forests-green-globe-climate-change/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"180\",\"title\":\"Russia - Countries \u0026 Regions - IEA\",\"description\":\"Russia is the world's second-largest producer of natural gas, behind the United States, and has the world's largest gas reserves.\",\"url\":\"https://www.iea.org/countries/russia\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"181\",\"title\":\"Russia Biodiversity: Animal and Plant Species and What Is Under ...\",\"description\":\"Dec 11, 2023 · It has 12,500 species of vascular plants, 320 species of mammals, over 732 species of birds, 75 species of reptiles, and about 30 species of ...\",\"url\":\"https://constructive-voices.com/russia-biodiversity/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"182\",\"title\":\"Animals of Russia - Animalia Bio\",\"description\":\"Russian biodiversity includes 12,500 species of vascular plants, 2,200 species ... Russian fauna is composed of 320 species of mammals, over 732 species of birds ...\",\"url\":\"https://animalia.bio/russia-animals\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"183\",\"title\":\"Russia Biodiversity and Nature Conservation | BioDB\",\"description\":\"The country is also remarkable in terms of animal species, with over 320 species of mammals, including iconic creatures like the Siberian tiger, brown bear, ...\",\"url\":\"https://biodb.com/region/russia/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"184\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Lake Baikal - UNESCO World Heritage Centre\",\"description\":\"Lake Baikal is the oldest and deepest lake, with 20% of the world's unfrozen freshwater, and is known as the 'Galapagos of Russia' with rich faunas. It is also ...\",\"url\":\"https://whc.unesco.org/document/163201\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"185\",\"title\":\"Will Russia's Forests Be an Asset or an Obstacle in Climate Fight?\",\"description\":\"Jul 15, 2021 · Most years, it turns out, Russia's boreal forests take up more carbon than is being lost to deforestation across the whole of the tropics. It ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://e360.yale.edu/features/will-russias-forests-be-an-asset-or-obstacle-in-the-climate-fight\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"186\",\"title\":\"Russia Has Most Protected Natural Areas in the World, WWF Says\",\"description\":\"3.3 times more than previously thought, the state-run RIA ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2019/05/20/russia-has-most-protected-natural-areas-in-the-world-wwf-says-a65659\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"187\",\"title\":\"Russia National Parks\",\"description\":\"Russia has a vast network of protected areas, including 64 national parks that cover approximately 95,000 square miles (245,000 square kilometers), which ...\",\"url\":\"https://nationalparksassociation.org/country/russia-national-parks/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"188\",\"title\":\"Protection of endangered species: Siberian tiger\",\"description\":\"Since 2010, the Russian Geographical Society has supported the Amur Tiger project. Its purpose is to study the state of the Amur tiger population, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.rgo.ru/en/projects/protection-and-study-endangered-species/protection-endangered-species-siberian-tiger\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"189\",\"title\":\"Saving the amur tiger - BBC Earth\",\"description\":\"Conservation efforts include anti-poaching, patrols, tougher laws, technology like cameras and AI, eco-corridors, and a \\\"Tiger Tunnel\\\" to help the Amur tiger.\",\"url\":\"https://www.bbcearth.com/news/saving-the-amur-tiger\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"190\",\"title\":\"Deforestation in Russia: Depleting the Lungs of the World | Earth.Org\",\"description\":\"Nov 19, 2020 · From 2001 to 2019, Russia lost 64 million hectares of relative tree cover, equivalent to an 8.4% decrease since 2000 and 17% of the global total ...\",\"url\":\"https://earth.org/deforestation-in-russia/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"191\",\"title\":\"Illegal Logging in the Russian Far East: Global Demand and Taiga\",\"description\":\"Apr 16, 2013 · The forests of the Russian Far East‚ – known as the \\\"Ussuri Taiga\\\"‚ – are being pushed to the brink of destruction due to pervasive, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.worldwildlife.org/publications/illegal-logging-in-the-russian-far-east-global-demand-and-taiga-destruction/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"192\",\"title\":\"Siberian fires having catastrophic effects on indigenous peoples and ...\",\"description\":\"Oct 15, 2019 · The world's largest forest–the Siberian Taiga in Russia–has been on fire for most of 2019, destroying indigenous peoples' livelihoods.\",\"url\":\"https://iwgia.org/en/russia/3516-siberian-fires-having-catastrophic-effects-on-indigenous-peoples-and-livelihoods.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"193\",\"title\":\"The Environmental Outlook in Russia - Intelligence Resource Program\",\"description\":\"Russia's leading environmental concern is water pollution. Municipalities are the main source of pollution, followed by industry and agriculture.\",\"url\":\"https://irp.fas.org/nic/environmental_outlook_russia.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"194\",\"title\":\"How Norilsk, in the Russian Arctic, became one of the most polluted ...\",\"description\":\"Dec 10, 2021 · Yet the warm, spring day when 6.5 million gallons of diesel fuel spilled from the Norilsk Nickel complex into the Daldykan River marked both the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nbcnews.com/news/world/norilsk-russian-arctic-became-one-polluted-places-earth-rcna6481\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"195\",\"title\":\"The Oil Spill From Russian Nickel Mine Is Moving Toward The Arctic ...\",\"description\":\"Jun 16, 2020 · Arctic watchers fear 150,000 barrels of diesel oil from a ruptured fuel tank at a Russian nickel mine will spill into the Arctic Ocean, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.npr.org/2020/06/16/878852931/the-oil-spill-from-russian-nickel-mine-is-moving-towards-the-arctic-ocean\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"196\",\"title\":\"Major Fuel Spill in Russia's North Spreads Toward Arctic Ocean\",\"description\":\"Jun 9, 2020 · The spill released about 150,000 barrels of diesel into a river, compared with about 260,000 barrels of crude oil released into Prince William ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/09/world/europe/russia-arctic-oil-spill.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"197\",\"title\":\"Sixty years of environmental change in the world's largest freshwater ...\",\"description\":\"High-resolution data collected over the past 60 years by a single family of Siberian scientists on Lake Baikal reveal significant warming of surface waters.Missing:  conservation | Show results with:conservation\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3597250/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"198\",\"title\":\"Oil Spill in Siberia: Are We Prepared for Permafrost Thaw?\",\"description\":\"Jun 11, 2020 · The spill started on May 29, when an oil tank collapsed near the city of Norilsk, most likely due to the thawing permafrost in the area.\",\"url\":\"https://www.thearcticinstitute.org/oil-spill-siberia-prepared-permafrost-thaw/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"199\",\"title\":\"Russia's hunting department assumes oversight of endangered ...\",\"description\":\"Jun 26, 2025 · Russia's Red Data Book (“Krasnaya Kniga”) is the country's official state document listing endangered and protected species of animals, plants, ...\",\"url\":\"https://theins.ru/en/news/282530\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"200\",\"title\":\"Does Russia stand to benefit from climate change? | News\",\"description\":\"Feb 21, 2024 · Environmental impacts already occurring in Russia include flooding, heat waves, drought and wildfires that affect not only communities, but ...\",\"url\":\"https://news.nd.edu/news/does-russia-stand-to-benefit-from-climate-change/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"201\",\"title\":\"The Constitution of the Russian Federation\",\"description\":\"We, the multinational people of the Russian Federation, united by a common fate on our land, establishing human rights and freedoms, civic peace and accord.\",\"url\":\"http://www.constitution.ru/en/10003000-01.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"202\",\"title\":\"Constitution of the Russian Federation\",\"description\":\"The Russian Federation - Russia is a democratic federative law-governed state with a republican form of government. 2. The names Russian Federation and Russia ...Missing:  semi- | Show results with:semi-\",\"url\":\"http://archive.government.ru/eng/gov/base/54.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"203\",\"title\":\"Chapter 4. The President of the Russian Federation\",\"description\":\"govern the foreign policy of the Russian Federation; · hold negotiations and sign international treaties and agreements of the Russian Federation; · sign ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.constitution.ru/en/10003000-05.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"204\",\"title\":\"President ∙ Structure ∙ President of Russia\",\"description\":\"The President shall resolve issues of citizenship of the Russian Federation, award state decorations and grant pardons.\",\"url\":\"http://www.en.kremlin.ru/structure/president\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"205\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Presidential Power in the Russian Constitution\",\"description\":\"An intermediate type, semi-presidentialism, has both a prime minister, dependent on the confidence of the parliament, and a popularly elected president.2 Semi- ...\",\"url\":\"https://ir.law.fsu.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1064\u0026context=jtlp\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"206\",\"title\":\"Political System\",\"description\":\"Russia is a democratic federal state with a republican form of government. The legislative body of the Russian Federation is the bicameral Federal Assembly ...\",\"url\":\"https://pekin.mid.ru/en/countries/rossiya/politicheskaya_sistema/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"207\",\"title\":\"The political system of the Russian Federation: President and ...\",\"description\":\"Nov 9, 2018 · The President of the Russian Federation determines the basic objectives of the internal and foreign policy of the State and represents the ...\",\"url\":\"http://duma.gov.ru/en/news/28748/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"208\",\"title\":\"Federal Constitutional Law on the Government of the Russian ...\",\"description\":\"The President of the Russian Federation ensures coordinated function and interaction between the Government of the Russian Federation and other state power ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"http://archive.government.ru/eng/gov/base/53.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"209\",\"title\":\"Referendum In Russia Passes, Allowing Putin To Remain President ...\",\"description\":\"Jul 1, 2020 · The vote approves constitutional changes, including a reset on presidential terms that will allow Putin to run twice more after his current ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.npr.org/2020/07/01/886440694/referendum-in-russia-passes-allowing-putin-to-remain-president-until-2036\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"210\",\"title\":\"Putin Signs Constitutional Changes That Allow Him To Rule Until 2036\",\"description\":\"Apr 5, 2021 · One of the constitutional changes resets Putin's term-limit clock to zero, allowing him to seek reelection when his current term expires in 2024 ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.rferl.org/a/putin-signs-law-to-rule-until-2036/31187934.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"211\",\"title\":\"The Interaction of Power Branches - President of Russia\",\"description\":\"The President shall be the head of state and the guarantor of the Constitution and of civil and human rights and liberties.\",\"url\":\"http://www.en.kremlin.ru/structure/president/authority/interaction\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"212\",\"title\":\"FACTBOX: Russian president and prime minister: who does what?\",\"description\":\"May 7, 2008 · - Guarantor of the constitution, citizens' rights. - Defender of Russia's sovereignty. - Prime minister reports directly to the president.\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.reuters.com/article/world/factbox-russian-president-and-prime-minister-who-does-what-idUSL07183254/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"213\",\"title\":\"Presidential Executive Office ∙ Structure ∙ President of Russia\",\"description\":\"The President oversees the general functioning of his Executive Office, but its day-to-day activities are managed by the Chief of Staff of the Presidential ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"http://www.en.kremlin.ru/structure/administration\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"214\",\"title\":\"Federal Assembly - President of Russia\",\"description\":\"The Federal Assembly of the Russian Federation is a permanent body with functions and powers divided between its two chambers: the State Duma (lower chamber) ...\",\"url\":\"http://en.special.kremlin.ru/catalog/glossary/91\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"215\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Russian Federation, State Duma Elections, 19 September 2021\",\"description\":\"Sep 19, 2021 · Voters will elect 450 deputies through a mixed electoral system with half of them elected in single-mandate constituencies under the first-past- ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.osce.org/files/f/documents/0/f/491066_0.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"216\",\"title\":\"Russian Federation State Duma September 2021 | Election results\",\"description\":\"United Russia, led by former Prime Minister Dmitry Medvedev (see note 1), retained an absolute majority in the 450-member State Duma, and now holds 326 seats.\",\"url\":\"https://data.ipu.org/parliament/RU/RU-LC01/election/RU-LC01-E20210919\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"217\",\"title\":\"About State Duma\",\"description\":\"Status and powers, composition and Regulations of the State Duma. The State Duma is one of the chambers of the Russian parliament, the Federal Assembly.\",\"url\":\"http://duma.gov.ru/en/duma/about/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"218\",\"titl